"`__FILE__` / `__LINE__` 传入 `switch_core_perform_*`，便于泄漏追踪。"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/06-c-runtime.md:89
#: 10a2b72d55114c3b98b061a81dda5a22
msgid "2. What APR/FSPR is for"
msgstr "2. APR/FSPR 扮演什么角色"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/06-c-runtime.md:91
#: 279b11171fb6478c89356eb3ae9c1edb
msgid ""
"Apache Portable Runtime (vendored as `libs/apr`, types prefixed `fspr_`) "
"abstracts OS primitives. FreeSWITCH does **not** treat Linux syscalls as "
"the programming model."
msgstr ""
"Apache Portable Runtime（vendored 在 `libs/apr`，类型前缀 `fspr_`）抽象 OS "
"原语。FreeSWITCH **并不**把 Linux syscall 当成自己的编程模型。"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/06-c-runtime.md:105
#: 9fc7541b54d44d068a8d019b85c0066c
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Sockets are a typical stack. `switch_socket_accept` in `src/switch_apr.c`"
" returns `fspr_socket_accept(...)`, which eventually calls the OS "
"`accept()`. `mod_event_socket` creates TCP sockets with "
"`switch_socket_create` "
"(`src/mod/event_handlers/mod_event_socket/mod_event_socket.c`). Version "
"pin: [Tech Stack](02-tech-stack.md) (`fspr_version.h`)."
msgstr ""
"Socket 是典型例子。`src/switch_apr.c` 里的 `switch_socket_accept` 返回 "
"`fspr_socket_accept(...)`，最终走到 OS 的 `accept()`。`mod_event_socket` 用 "
"`switch_socket_create` 建 TCP "
"socket（`src/mod/event_handlers/mod_event_socket/mod_event_socket.c`）。版本见 "
"[Tech Stack](03-tech-stack.md)（`fspr_version.h`）。"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/06-c-runtime.md:107
#: c3005e09bf3c4981a35271b16bbc0947
msgid "3. Core is more than APR"
msgstr "3. Core 不只是“用了 APR”"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/06-c-runtime.md:124
#: cce52e98af124ad7a558e84086ea3f30
msgid ""
"FSPR does not know what a SIP INVITE or an Opus frame is. That is core + "
"modules."
msgstr "FSPR 不知道 SIP INVITE 或 Opus 帧是什么。那是 core 与模块的事。"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/06-c-runtime.md:126
#: d5b4b092e902490c933a949e327c86b6
msgid "4. Memory pools"
msgstr "4. 内存管理：Memory Pool"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/06-c-runtime.md:128
#: e1e0b2c1a1244986aefd29542a8b7a64
msgid ""
"Implementation: `src/switch_core_memory.c`. Create/destroy macros: "
"`switch_core_new_memory_pool` / `switch_core_destroy_memory_pool`."
msgstr ""
"实现：`src/switch_core_memory.c`。创建/销毁宏：`switch_core_new_memory_pool` / "
"`switch_core_destroy_memory_pool`。"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/06-c-runtime.md:130
#: 3934ef309b1d45e284b09591902010b4
msgid ""
"Pattern used in modules (example: profile structs allocated from a "
"module-owned pool):"
msgstr "模块里常见的写法（例如从模块自己的 pool 分配 profile）："

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/06-c-runtime.md:140
#: 93bd76acb56f4842b272986a51ce41f6
msgid ""
"Destroying the pool frees every allocation from that pool. That matches a"
" **call/session lifetime boundary** better than pairing every `malloc` "
"with a `free`."
msgstr ""
"销毁 pool 会释放该 pool 上的全部分配。这比给每一次 `malloc` 配对 `free` 更符合 **呼叫/session "
"的生命周期边界**。"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/06-c-runtime.md:142
#: f9c0d77e475e49deb3e31dae3962cdde
msgid ""
"A SIP call creates a session, channel, RTP, codecs, variables, and "
"events. On hangup the session pool goes away instead of walking a free-"
"list of dozens of objects. Leaks, double-frees, and use-after-free still "
"happen if you stash a pointer after the pool is gone, or allocate from "
"the wrong pool."
msgstr ""
"一次 SIP 呼叫会创建 session、channel、RTP、codec、变量和 event。挂机时销毁 session "
"pool，而不是逐个走几十个对象的 free 列表。若在 pool 销毁后仍握着指针，或从错误的 pool 分配，仍然会出现泄漏、double "
"free、use-after-free。"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/06-c-runtime.md:144
#: dcd792731b4642dead6d3f1c58b66673
msgid "5. Session is the main lifetime"
msgstr "5. Session 是理解内存管理的关键"

