#: bf7adb2c7cd8491e888d9933d6fc288f
msgid ""
"**The design center is not “how to malloc in C.” It is “how a call’s many"
" objects share a clear lifetime.”** Hangup destroys the session pool; the"
" attached channel, codec contexts, queues, and frames go with it. "
"APR/FSPR is POSIX-like portability. Core is the realtime-communications "
"OS on top."
msgstr ""
"**设计核心不是“如何在 C 里管理 malloc”，而是“如何让复杂实时通信对象拥有清晰的生命周期”。** 挂机销毁 session "
"pool，其上的 channel、codec context、queue、frame 一并回收。APR/FSPR 是 POSIX "
"式可移植层；Core 则是其上专门服务实时通信的操作系统。"

